WEBVTT

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:07.960
<i>Once, I was forced to participate in 
a parade for the Balsteros Empire.</i>

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:14.950
<i>I waved, as they wanted me to.</i>

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:20.710
<i>But the people outside seemed cold somehow.</i>

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:23.940
<i>What I remember much better</i>

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:27.340
<i>is my mother's profile, as she sat beside me.</i>

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:32.940
<i>In the palace, I had barely 
any time with her at all,</i>

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.500
<i>so I was very happy.</i>

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:37.540
<i>This was back when I was still Karl La Hire,</i>

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:42.400
<i>crown prince of the empire.</i>

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:21.160
<b>Episode 3: 
The Wind Revolution</b>

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:21.210
Everyone, let's eat!

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:27.150
Wh-What is this strange dish?

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:29.760
The Albus family special curry!

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.480
My older sisters taught me the recipe.

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:34.610
Eat it while it's hot.

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:46.560
A-Are you okay?

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:51.730
It's delicious!

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:56.780
It really is great!

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:01.990
Even though I'm worn out from training, 
it stimulates the appetite.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.300
Does it?

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:07.580
It's still really tough, training every day.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:10.640
I wish they'd take it easy on us a bit!

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:11.970
That's true...

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:16.030
I had no idea the flight school here was so tough.

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:20.880
Even I've lost some weight.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:24.270
Eh?!

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.040
Where?

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:28.640
Your face is getting a little thinner, Mitty.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:30.040
Around the cheeks.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:34.980
I'd p-prefer if you wouldn't call me that...

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:37.600
He's blushing!

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:39.620
This looks like such fun.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:42.890
So you all live together like this all the time?

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:43.710
Yeah.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:46.260
Want another helping, Claire?

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:49.450
Ari's lazy, but her cooking—

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:51.050
I'm not lazy!

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:53.640
Kal, you always...

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:02.690
It's good!

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:07.610
What's his problem?

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.260
Claire's being nice enough to talk to him.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:12.430
Is he always like that during training?

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:14.080
Aren't you partnered with him, Ari?

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:15.460
Yeah.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:19.400
His piloting isn't great, and he doesn't seem 
interested in shooting rifles at all.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:24.240
Why did Ignacio decide to attend 
this school, anyway?

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:25.340
I don't know.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:29.720
I'm sorry...

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:31.800
I need to get home.

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:35.230
Oh, yeah. You have a curfew, right?

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:37.880
I'll s-see you halfway there!

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:39.680
I'll be fine.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:41.890
Oh...

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:44.910
Thanks for the curry.

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:46.270
It was great.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:49.160
Thanks, I'll make it again, so come back!

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:49.900
I will.

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:53.740
Kal-el... Everyone, see you tomorrow!

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:55.330
See you tomorrow!

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:02.040
What?

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:04.940
Sure you don't want to follow her?

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:08.860
Seriously, what's the deal 
between you two?

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:11.570
The deal—

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:14.000
He's covered in sweat.

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:16.110
It's nothing...

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:20.090
There's no way Claire would 
be interested in this wimp.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:22.090
You're pretty rude

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:23.720
for a little sister.

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:27.000
And you're my little brother.

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:28.530
Little sister!

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:29.580
Little brother!

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:34.520
So which of these two is actually older?

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:35.840
No idea...

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:38.090
It remains a mystery.

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:41.230
Sh-Shizuka?

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:42.270
When did you arrive?

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:44.060
Don't mind me.

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:49.070
I'm just observing an eye on you kids.

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:52.320
I mean, keeping an eye on you.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:55.860
This has been an interesting 
meal in numerous ways.

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:11.100
How is your mission as an instructor going?

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:13.800
It's quite tiring to send others into the air.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:16.220
It's far easier to simply fly yourself.

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:18.290
I read your report.

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:21.620
I want them to start training to fly in formation.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:23.790
But, sir...

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:26.220
They haven't even been in school a month.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:28.880
They haven't acquired the skill for formations...

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:30.480
Now that they're on Isla,

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:32.730
we can't go easy on them, 
even if they are students.

00:06:33.070 --> 00:06:36.090
Ensure they understand dogfighting basics 
before we reach the Holy Spring.

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:37.330
But...

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:40.970
In the end, that is what will save their lives.

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:43.710
Admiral Luis believes this.

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:46.540
The Admiral...

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:05.530
They're in a real hurry.

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:09.870
The brass don't think of them as real, do they?

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:15.360
Whatever the reasons, we must 
train them to be full pilots.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:19.580
I'm sure you don't disagree with that.

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:30.800
Th-The wind's buffeting my rifle...

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:34.840
Bring the center of gravity toward yourself.

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:39.230
Lean forward, and pull the rifle toward you.

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:41.590
Like this?

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:49.210
I get it.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:50.610
Thanks, Claire!

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:59.240
I'm sorry... We're out of ammo.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:00.850
I see.

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:03.740
Okay, I'll land.

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:07.520
Let's do our best tomorrow, Kal-el.

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:14.220
That was pathetic, Kal-el Albus.

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:15.710
Fausto...

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:17.590
It isn't too late.

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:19.410
Find another partner.

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:24.090
It wasn't ever possible a pair from the 
Centezual and Van Whyl classes

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:26.480
could work together.

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:29.270
I'll be waiting for you,

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:32.560
Miss Claire.

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:38.410
Stop hitting on her!

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:41.270
You fluffy-headed jerk!

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:44.580
Don't ignore me!

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:47.100
You can see the difference between 
a commoner and a noble.

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:50.190
But he does seem like a commoner!

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:53.380
Noriaki doesn't seem that important.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:55.930
Don't agree with that!

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:58.170
The irrelevant guy is mad!

00:08:57.790 --> 00:08:58.850
Don't call me that!

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:00.800
The irrelevant guy is irrelevant!

00:08:59.110 --> 00:08:59.950
Kal-el...

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:00.800
I'm not irrelevant!

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:01.850
I am not!

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.540
Irrelevant! Irrelevant! Irrelevant!

00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:04.050
It doesn't bother me.

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:03.970
I am not! Stop calling me that!

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:04.020
Irrelevant! Irrelevant! Irrelevant!

00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:04.600
I'm not!

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:05.400
You are!

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:06.020
I'm not!

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:06.600
You are!

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:08.670
Thank you, Claire.

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:12.310
I guess there are people like that,

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:14.790
who really act like noble-born children.

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:18.700
The Melze family is one of the 
most important in Balsteros.

00:09:19.060 --> 00:09:23.210
I heard the commander of the knights, Leopold, 
was a hero in the Wind Rebellion.

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:25.290
That's right!

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:28.700
Speaking of the Wind Revolution, 
have you heard the rumor?

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:30.460
I heard it in Centezual.

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:35.480
The former crown prince of Balsteros, Karl La Hire,

00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:38.910
might have sneaked on board Isla.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:42.840
And he wants revenge against Nina Viento.

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:51.170
No way!

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:53.130
You don't believe it, Wolf?

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:56.690
What do you think? You're from Balsteros.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:02.640
It's impossible...

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:07.440
Crown Prince Karl died during the 
Wind Revolution, didn't he?

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:09.240
That's right.

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:11.840
You'll have to come up with 
a better story, Nanako.

00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:14.410
Wh-What? Don't make fun of me!

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:17.460
That's right... Karl La Hire 
died a long time ago.

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:16.410
This is in return for earlier!

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:18.710
Yeah.

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:29.270
<i>Mother...</i>

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:33.410
<i>The Wind Revolution...</i>

00:10:34.470 --> 00:10:37.440
<i>The rebellion six years ago that turned Balsteros</i>

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:39.840
<i>from an empire into a republic.</i>

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:48.190
<i>If only that night had never happened, 
my real parents would still...</i>

00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:56.960
Rebels are approaching the palace.

00:10:57.630 --> 00:10:59.540
Controlling them from behind the scenes...

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:07.870
...is Frontier Duke Ameriano.

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:17.610
The flying warship El Aguila... 
The capital's protector!

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:48.390
What's happening?

00:12:12.530 --> 00:12:15.280
So this is the power of the 
Priestess of Saint Aldista?

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:20.900
It's as if the wind were singing 
a song of destruction.

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:37.810
It took a hundred years, but you 
finally achieved your revenge,

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:38.850
Ameriano.

00:12:39.350 --> 00:12:41.690
Now that the throne has burned 
to ash, are you satisfied?

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:46.670
It was the people who brought you down, Gregorio.

00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:53.990
This is the beloved daughter of Saint Aldista,

00:12:53.990 --> 00:12:55.670
the priestess who controls the wind...

00:12:56.840 --> 00:12:58.540
Nina Viento.

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:01.780
You would mock Aldista's name,

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:04.470
giving it to this country girl and her tricks?

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:05.260
You bastard!

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:07.670
The emperor insulted the priestess of the wind!

00:13:07.670 --> 00:13:09.300
Beg for forgiveness!

00:13:09.740 --> 00:13:11.300
Bow your head!

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:14.830
Stop it... Know your place!

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:15.390
Karl!

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:17.150
You, too!

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:18.400
M-Mother!

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:19.820
Mother!

00:13:20.340 --> 00:13:21.340
The princess!

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:23.160
Make the prince bow, too!

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:25.470
Let me go! Let me go!

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:44.200
You've finally calmed down.

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:50.240
Nina...

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:55.370
Nina Viento!

00:13:57.930 --> 00:14:01.750
Let the bloodline of the king abide,

00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:04.490
for the day when you desire a king once more!

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:10.720
<i>The Balsteros Empire fell in a single night,</i>

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:13.330
<i>to be replaced by a republic.</i>

00:14:14.420 --> 00:14:16.720
<i>Mother and I were imprisoned.</i>

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:18.960
<i>And then...</i>

00:14:23.490 --> 00:14:24.550
Karl,

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:28.820
no matter what happens, promise me 
you won't hate anyone.

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:33.420
Hatred will only destroy you.

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:35.980
You must forgive them,

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:39.290
no matter what horrible things they do to you.

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:43.560
I'm sure that is your role,

00:14:44.350 --> 00:14:45.980
the task you have been given.

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:51.200
I don't understand!

00:14:56.170 --> 00:14:57.260
"I forgive you."

00:14:57.260 --> 00:14:58.190
Say it.

00:15:08.410 --> 00:15:09.370
I forgive you...

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:11.580
That's right.

00:15:11.810 --> 00:15:13.370
If you forgive,

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:15.340
the light will wipe away the darkness.

00:15:15.840 --> 00:15:19.350
If I forgive, the light will wipe away the darkness?

00:15:23.510 --> 00:15:24.620
It's time.

00:15:25.140 --> 00:15:25.820
Yes.

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:28.280
Karl, no—

00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:29.860
Karl...

00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:31.410
Mother!

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:35.830
We'll always be together.

00:15:37.260 --> 00:15:40.410
I'll be here forever.

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:47.070
Mother...

00:15:48.490 --> 00:15:49.540
Mother!

00:15:55.380 --> 00:15:58.410
Why are you leaving me alone?

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:00.320
Karl...

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:06.230
No, you mustn't!

00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:07.860
Karl!

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:14.660
Whore!

00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:19.020
You belong in a pig cart!

00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:23.720
Mother!

00:16:26.470 --> 00:16:27.360
Mother!

00:16:30.310 --> 00:16:32.050
Mother!

00:16:44.530 --> 00:16:45.910
Nina Viento...

00:16:47.070 --> 00:16:48.470
It's her fault!

00:16:50.250 --> 00:16:53.780
I'll never forgive her!

00:16:59.530 --> 00:17:00.470
Mother...

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:06.910
You promised you'd fly with me...

00:17:08.560 --> 00:17:09.970
Hey, warden...

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:12.100
Is that the prince?

00:17:12.570 --> 00:17:14.540
He doesn't look so good...

00:17:15.530 --> 00:17:18.350
We can't send a child to the guillotine.

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:19.960
They tried to sicken him, so he'd die.

00:17:19.960 --> 00:17:21.550
That's horrible.

00:17:21.550 --> 00:17:23.400
And you're okay with this?

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:28.640
Hey, wait!

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:33.380
The prince died today, shortly after his mother.

00:17:34.230 --> 00:17:38.230
You're in a position to make everyone 
believe that, aren't you?

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:39.890
I...

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:48.930
...want him to fly!

00:17:57.960 --> 00:17:59.120
Kal-el?

00:18:12.490 --> 00:18:14.610
So it's my turn to pilot today, huh?

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:16.580
Let's do this, Claire.

00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:19.070
Kal-el, um...

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:22.810
No, never mind...

00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:24.330
They're starting.

00:18:24.690 --> 00:18:25.460
Let's hurry.

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:31.250
Today, we'll be practicing recon patrols.

00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:35.720
This will be your first flight in 
formation, away from Isla.

00:18:35.720 --> 00:18:37.720
Don't lower your guard.

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:38.490
Yes, sir!

00:18:39.230 --> 00:18:41.720
Will Kal-el be okay?

00:18:42.980 --> 00:18:47.350
Sonia, why did you put Kal-el 
in with the first class?

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:50.930
They've been fighting a lot...

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:53.360
This is a chance for them to get along.

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:01.940
Split up.

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:04.240
Establish a recon line.

00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:14.510
Kal-el, be careful.

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:17.210
The clouds are getting thicker.

00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:20.970
The wind's strong, and it's 
throwing everyone off course.

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:24.080
I wish they'd try harder to avoid the clouds...

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:26.220
Yeah, I'm a little worried.

00:19:28.110 --> 00:19:29.640
Claire, get inside!

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:30.270
Right!

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:37.280
They're doing that deliberately...

00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:44.330
Kal-el, up ahead!

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:53.660
I can't see anything...

00:19:54.230 --> 00:19:55.310
Stay calm.

00:19:56.030 --> 00:19:58.770
Claire, am I turning?

00:19:58.770 --> 00:20:02.700
Check your attitude indicator and turn coordinator to see what the plane is doing.

00:20:03.290 --> 00:20:04.220
R-Right.

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:21.060
Th-The instruments!

00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:24.450
Trust your attitude indicator, Kal-el!

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:26.830
You're suffering from spatial disorientation.

00:20:28.170 --> 00:20:29.910
Trust the El Halcon.

00:20:29.910 --> 00:20:32.790
It's okay! You're moving straight ahead.

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:34.590
Damn.

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:38.420
You're right, aren't you?

00:20:41.780 --> 00:20:42.790
We did it...

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:44.320
There's a gap in the clouds!

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:46.910
We're okay now!

00:20:56.760 --> 00:20:58.140
We've been separated

00:20:59.530 --> 00:21:00.810
from everyone.

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:03.480
Looks that way...

00:21:05.430 --> 00:21:07.450
We should land on the water.

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:11.940
I can't navigate, so I don't know 
how to get us back to Isla.

00:21:12.610 --> 00:21:13.550
But...

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:17.570
Understood, we'll land.

00:21:32.710 --> 00:21:35.000
It's my fault... I'm sorry.

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:37.150
That isn't true.

00:21:37.150 --> 00:21:39.860
It isn't only your fault.

00:21:40.410 --> 00:21:43.500
We're a team, so we both failed.

00:21:43.500 --> 00:21:44.660
Claire...

00:21:54.650 --> 00:21:55.940
It's going to storm.

